# An element of a view is a number, or undefined past the end. `*`, `-`, `/` turn both operands into numerics, and a number or undefined turns without running anything:
# it is turned in front, and the operator stands beside ONE NUMBER: the other value is asked in line whether it is a number; the stub is the rare way. Both operands went boxed to the stub of the generic form.
# `+` is left as it was: undefined + "x" is a text.
# f1 = times, f2 = less, f3 = plus
# RUN: walk f1:Body mechanisms=all
# CHECK: = GetTypedArrayElement
# CHECK: number {{*}}= ToNumber
# CHECK: = Mul {{*}}form=NumberAndValue
# RUN(LESS): walk f2:Body mechanisms=all
# LESS: = GetTypedArrayElement
# LESS: number {{*}}= ToNumber
# LESS: = Sub {{*}}form=NumberAndValue
# RUN(PLUS): walk f3:Body mechanisms=all
# PLUS: = GetTypedArrayElement
# PLUS-NOT: = ToNumber
# PLUS: = Add {{*}}form=Generic
# RUN(SHELL): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# SHELL: 4.5 NaN 5 NaN 4.5 NaN
# SHELL-NEXT: 6 NaN 6 NaN 1.54 undefined4
# SHELL-NEXT: 0 NaN 2 NaN 1.5 NaN
# SHELL-NEXT: 7.5 NaN 7 NaN 1.55 undefined5
# SHELL-NEXT: exited with 0
